	// HYPOTHESIS-2: Increasing the cubic term coefficient from 0.1 to 0.14 will reduce avg_p95_ms below 5150 by creating even stronger tail differentiation without hurting mean latency
	// MECHANISM-2: The confirmed H1 showed cubic helps P95. Going slightly stronger (0.14 vs 0.1) should push P95 lower while loadWeight adaptation keeps mean stable.
	// EXPECT-2: avg_p95_ms < 5150
